IMPORT prelude

§ `CODEX INSURANCE LIMITED — hospitalization policy`

-- Isomorphic encoding of the fixture at inputs/chubb-policy.txt. Section numbers
-- below (1.1, 1.2, 1.3, 2.1, 3.1-3.6) match the numbering in that document.
--
-- Two standing assumptions, per the task brief, are NOT modelled as fields or
-- conjuncts anywhere below:
--   * the agreement has been signed;
--   * the premium for the policy period has been paid, on time.
-- Both are items 1-2 of §1.1's four-part test; only items 3-4 (the §1.3
-- condition, and non-cancelation) vary from claim to claim, so only those two
-- are represented in `policy in effect at time of hospitalization`.
--
-- All times are NUMBERs of months elapsed since the policy's effective date
-- (0 = the effective date itself), never absolute dates — the effective date
-- itself never needs representing, only offsets from it, per the task brief.

§§ `The Claim record — the facts a query must supply`

DECLARE Claim HAS
    `month of hospitalization`                            IS A NUMBER
    `age at hospitalization`                               IS A NUMBER
    `caused by skydiving`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused by military service`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused by firefighter service`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused by police service`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `month of the wellness visit`                          IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `month the wellness visit confirmation was supplied`   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `guilty of fraud, misrepresentation, or withholding`   IS A BOOLEAN

-- Notes on the four "caused by ..." flags: §2.1 excludes an event "arising
-- directly or indirectly out of" the named service or activity — a causal
-- test, not a status test. A claimant who merely *holds* one of these
-- occupations "at the time" of an unrelated hospitalization does not trip the
-- exclusion; the hospitalizing event itself must arise out of the service.
-- Each flag therefore records that causal fact directly, and it is for the
-- query (in apply.l4) to decide, from the fact pattern, whether it is TRUE.

§§ `1.3 — the wellness-visit condition`

-- "No later than the 7th month anniversary ... you will supply us with
--  written confirmation ... of a wellness visit ... occurring no later than
--  the 6th month anniversary ..."
-- This bundles two deadlines into one compliance act: the visit itself
-- (<= 6 months) and the confirmation of it reaching the insurer (<= 7
-- months). Until the 7-month deadline arrives, the condition is "still
-- pending" (§1.1 item 3) even though nothing has yet been supplied.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `wellness visit occurred timely` claim IS
    CONSIDER visitMonth
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        -- the visit's own date was not part of this query's fact pattern;
        -- unrelated to whatever is being tested, so treated as satisfied
    WHEN JUST vm THEN vm AT MOST 6
    WHERE
        visitMonth MEANS claim's `month of the wellness visit`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `condition 1.3 pending or satisfied` claim IS
    CONSIDER confirmationMonth
    WHEN NOTHING THEN claim's `month of hospitalization` LESS THAN 7
        -- nothing supplied yet, but the 7-month deadline has not passed
        -- either, so the condition is still pending, not yet breached
    WHEN JUST cm THEN
            cm AT MOST 7
        AND `wellness visit occurred timely` claim
    WHERE
        confirmationMonth MEANS claim's `month the wellness visit confirmation was supplied`

§§ `1.2 — cancelation`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `policy canceled` claim IS
        -- fraud, or any misrepresentation or material withholding of information
        claim's `guilty of fraud, misrepresentation, or withholding`
    OR  -- the §1.3 condition was not satisfied in a timely fashion
        NOT (`condition 1.3 pending or satisfied` claim)
    OR  -- automatically canceled at the end of the one-year policy term (§3.6)
        claim's `month of hospitalization` AT LEAST 12

§§ `1.1 — policy in effect and conditions`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `policy in effect at time of hospitalization` claim IS
        `condition 1.3 pending or satisfied` claim
    AND NOT `policy canceled` claim

§§ `2.1 — general exclusions`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `excluded event` claim IS
        -- 1. Skydiving
        claim's `caused by skydiving`
    OR  -- 2. Service in the military
        claim's `caused by military service`
    OR  -- 3. Service as a fire fighter
        claim's `caused by firefighter service`
    OR  -- 4. Service in the police
        claim's `caused by police service`
    OR  -- 5. age at the time of the hospitalization is equal to or greater than 80
        claim's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST 80

§§ `3.1 — territorial scope`

-- "Your Policy insures You twenty-four (24) hours a day anywhere in the
--  world." There is no territorial exclusion to encode: being abroad, or at
--  any particular hour, never removes coverage.

§§ `3.2-3.5 — arbitration, governing law, currency, premium`

-- Dispute-resolution mechanics (§3.2), choice of law (§3.3), currency of
-- payment (§3.4), and the lump-sum timing of the premium (§3.5) govern how a
-- dispute is resolved and how money moves, not whether a given
-- hospitalization event is one the policy covers. No rule is derived from
-- them for `covered` below.

§§ `3.6 — policy term`

-- "will last for a period of one year from [the effective] date" — captured
-- above as the `AT LEAST 12` disjunct of `policy canceled`.

§§ `Top-level decision`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `covered` claim IS
        `policy in effect at time of hospitalization` claim
    AND NOT `excluded event` claim
